IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa5-director-supplementary.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 10, Chapter 9, "Supplementary provisions": ss 247 to 249 (provision for employees, minutes of directors'
-- meetings, minutes as evidence) and ss 258 to 259 (power to increase financial limits, transactions under foreign law): lines 3264-3292 and 3369-3376 of
-- ukpga-2006-46.txt. The meaning of "director", "shadow director", "connected" and "controlling" (ss 250 to 257) is in coa5-director-definitions.l4.
--
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; not the official text.
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: see coa5-loans-exceptions.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING as the rule of 2026-10-29 reads them).

§ `Chapter 9: provision for employees on cessation or transfer of business (s 247)`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 247 Power to make provision for employees on cessation or transfer of business
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:3267 | (1) The powers of the directors of a company include (if they would not otherwise do so) power to make provision for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company, or any of its subsidiaries, in connection with the cessation or the transfer to any person of the whole or part of the undertaking of the company or that subsidiary.
@ref s 247(1) the power (src:3267-3267)
GIVEN `the provision is for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company, or any of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made in connection with the cessation or the transfer to any person of the whole or part of the undertaking of the company or that subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 247(1) the powers of the directors include the power to make the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision is for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company, or any of its subsidiaries`
       AND `it is made in connection with the cessation or the transfer to any person of the whole or part of the undertaking of the company or that subsidiary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "power to make provision for the benefit of persons employed or formerly employed by the company, or any of its subsidiaries, in connection with the cessation or the transfer to any person of the whole or part of the undertaking"

-- src:3268 | (2) This power is exercisable notwithstanding the general duty imposed by section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company).
@ref s 247(2) section 172 does not stand in the way (src:3268-3268)
GIVEN `s 247(1) the powers of the directors include the power to make the provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 247(2) the general duty in section 172 prevents the exercise of the power` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 247(1) the powers of the directors include the power to make the provision`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This power is exercisable notwithstanding the general duty imposed by section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company)"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This power is exercisable notwithstanding the general duty"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This power is exercisable notwithstanding the general duty"

-- src:3269 | (3) In the case of a company that is a charity it is exercisable notwithstanding any restrictions on the directors' powers (or the company's capacity) flowing from the objects of the company.
@ref s 247(3) charities (src:3269-3269)
GIVEN `s 247(1) the powers of the directors include the power to make the provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is a charity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 247(3) a restriction flowing from the company's objects prevents the exercise of the power` MEANS
    IF `s 247(1) the powers of the directors include the power to make the provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the company is a charity`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a company that is a charity it is exercisable notwithstanding any restrictions on the directors' powers (or the company's capacity) flowing from the objects of the company"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company that is a charity"

-- (5): a resolution of the directors must be authorised by the articles and does not sanction payments to or for the benefit of directors, former directors or shadow directors.
-- src:3274 | (5) A resolution of the directors—
-- src:3275 | (a) must be authorised by the company's articles, and
-- src:3276 | (b) is not sufficient sanction for payments to or for the benefit of directors, former directors or shadow directors.
@ref s 247(5) a resolution of the directors (src:3274-3276)
GIVEN `the resolution of the directors is authorised by the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments are to or for the benefit of directors, former directors or shadow directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 247(5) the resolution of the directors is sufficient sanction` MEANS
    IF `the resolution of the directors is authorised by the company's articles` AND (NOT `the payments are to or for the benefit of directors, former directors or shadow directors`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resolution of the directors— (a) must be authorised by the company's articles, and (b) is not sufficient sanction for payments to or for the benefit of directors, former directors or shadow directors"

-- src:3270 | (4) The power may only be exercised if sanctioned—
-- src:3271 | (a) by a resolution of the company, or
-- src:3272 | (b) by a resolution of the directors,
-- src:3273 | in accordance with the following provisions.
@ref s 247(4) sanction (src:3270-3273)
GIVEN `the power is sanctioned by a resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 247(5) the resolution of the directors is sufficient sanction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 247(4) the power may be exercised` MEANS
    IF `the power is sanctioned by a resolution of the company` OR `s 247(5) the resolution of the directors is sufficient sanction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The power may only be exercised if sanctioned— (a) by a resolution of the company, or (b) by a resolution of the directors, in accordance with the following provisions"

-- src:3277 | (6) Any other requirements of the company's articles as to the exercise of the power conferred by this section must be complied with.
@ref s 247(6) other requirements of the articles (src:3277-3277)
GIVEN `any other requirements of the company's articles as to the exercise of the power have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 247(6) the other requirements of the articles have been complied with` MEANS
    IF `any other requirements of the company's articles as to the exercise of the power have been complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any other requirements of the company's articles as to the exercise of the power conferred by this section must be complied with" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-MUST-1)

-- src:3278 | (7) Any payment under this section must be made—
-- src:3279 | (a) before the commencement of any winding up of the company, and
-- src:3280 | (b) out of profits of the company that are available for dividend.
@ref s 247(7) the payment (src:3278-3280)
GIVEN `the payment is made before the commencement of any winding up of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is made out of profits of the company that are available for dividend` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 247(7) the payment may be made` MEANS
    IF `the payment is made before the commencement of any winding up of the company` AND `the payment is made out of profits of the company that are available for dividend`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any payment under this section must be made— (a) before the commencement of any winding up of the company, and (b) out of profits of the company that are available for dividend" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-MUST-1)

§ `Records of meetings of directors (ss 248 and 249)`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 248 Minutes of directors' meetings
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:3283 | (1) Every company must cause minutes of all proceedings at meetings of its directors to be recorded.
@ref s 248(1) minutes (src:3283-3283)
GIVEN `minutes of all proceedings at meetings of the company's directors have been recorded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 248(1) the company has caused minutes of all proceedings at meetings of its directors to be recorded` MEANS
    IF `minutes of all proceedings at meetings of the company's directors have been recorded`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every company must cause minutes of all proceedings at meetings of its directors to be recorded" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-MUST-1)

DECLARE `s 248 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 248(1) cause minutes of all proceedings at meetings of the directors to be recorded`

-- The duty as a rule. The text states no time for it: none is invented (no WITHIN).
-- src:3283 | (1) Every company must cause minutes of all proceedings at meetings of its directors to be recorded.
@ref s 248(1) the duty (src:3283-3283)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 248 action`
`s 248(1) the company's duty to cause minutes to be recorded` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 248(1) cause minutes of all proceedings at meetings of the directors to be recorded`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 248(1): minutes of the proceedings at a meeting of the directors were not recorded (an offence by every officer in default, s 248(3))"

-- "at least ten years from the date of the meeting": on or before the date ten years on the records must still be kept (F-228-1: the anniversary day is counted in).
-- src:3284 | (2) The records must be kept for at least ten years from the date of the meeting.
@ref s 248(2) ten years (src:3284-3284)
GIVEN `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the date in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 248(2) the records must still be kept on the date` MEANS
    IF `the date in question` AT MOST `add years` `the date of the meeting` 10
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The records must be kept for at least ten years from the date of the meeting" (the period the text fixes has ended)

-- src:3285 | (3) If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 248(3) the offence (src:3285-3285)
GIVEN `s 248(1) the company has caused minutes of all proceedings at meetings of its directors to be recorded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has kept the records for at least ten years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 248(3) the officer commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 248(1) the company has caused minutes of all proceedings at meetings of its directors to be recorded` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the company recorded the minutes is not known
        IF `s 248(1) the company has caused minutes of all proceedings at meetings of its directors to be recorded` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the company has kept the records for at least ten years`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed" (the company complied)
        IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121's answer
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default"

-- src:3286 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 248(4) the penalty (src:3286-3286)
`s 248(4) the penalty` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 249 Minutes as evidence
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:3288 | (1) Minutes recorded in accordance with section 248, if purporting to be authenticated by the chairman of the meeting or by the chairman of the next directors' meeting, are evidence (in Scotland, sufficient evidence) of the proceedings at the meeting.
@ref s 249(1) minutes are evidence (src:3288-3288)
GIVEN `the minutes were recorded in accordance with section 248` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minutes purport to be authenticated by the chairman of the meeting or by the chairman of the next directors' meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 249(1) the minutes are evidence of the proceedings at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the minutes were recorded in accordance with section 248` AND `the minutes purport to be authenticated by the chairman of the meeting or by the chairman of the next directors' meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Minutes recorded in accordance with section 248, if purporting to be authenticated by the chairman of the meeting or by the chairman of the next directors' meeting, are evidence of the proceedings at the meeting" (this subsection makes them no evidence on these facts)

-- src:3288 | (1) Minutes recorded in accordance with section 248, if purporting to be authenticated by the chairman of the meeting or by the chairman of the next directors' meeting, are evidence (in Scotland, sufficient evidence) of the proceedings at the meeting.
@ref s 249(1) sufficient evidence in Scotland (src:3288-3288)
GIVEN `s 249(1) the minutes are evidence of the proceedings at the meeting` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 249(1) the minutes are sufficient evidence of the proceedings at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `s 249(1) the minutes are evidence of the proceedings at the meeting` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the proceedings are in Scotland`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "are evidence (in Scotland, sufficient evidence) of the proceedings at the meeting"

-- (2): "until the contrary is proved" (an input), where minutes have been made in accordance with s 248 of the proceedings of a meeting of directors.
-- src:3289 | (2) Where minutes have been made in accordance with that section of the proceedings of a meeting of directors, then, until the contrary is proved—
-- src:3290 | (a) the meeting is deemed duly held and convened,
-- src:3291 | (b) all proceedings at the meeting are deemed to have duly taken place, and
-- src:3292 | (c) all appointments at the meeting are deemed valid.
@ref s 249(2)(a) the meeting is deemed duly held and convened (src:3289-3292)
GIVEN `minutes have been made in accordance with section 248 of the proceedings of a meeting of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 249(2)(a) the meeting is deemed duly held and convened` MEANS
    IF `minutes have been made in accordance with section 248 of the proceedings of a meeting of directors` AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where minutes have been made in accordance with that section of the proceedings of a meeting of directors, then, until the contrary is proved— (a) the meeting is deemed duly held and convened"

-- src:3289 | (2) Where minutes have been made in accordance with that section of the proceedings of a meeting of directors, then, until the contrary is proved—
-- src:3290 | (a) the meeting is deemed duly held and convened,
-- src:3291 | (b) all proceedings at the meeting are deemed to have duly taken place, and
-- src:3292 | (c) all appointments at the meeting are deemed valid.
@ref s 249(2)(b) all proceedings are deemed to have duly taken place (src:3289-3292)
GIVEN `minutes have been made in accordance with section 248 of the proceedings of a meeting of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 249(2)(b) all proceedings at the meeting are deemed to have duly taken place` MEANS
    IF `minutes have been made in accordance with section 248 of the proceedings of a meeting of directors` AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the contrary is proved— ... (b) all proceedings at the meeting are deemed to have duly taken place"

-- src:3289 | (2) Where minutes have been made in accordance with that section of the proceedings of a meeting of directors, then, until the contrary is proved—
-- src:3290 | (a) the meeting is deemed duly held and convened,
-- src:3291 | (b) all proceedings at the meeting are deemed to have duly taken place, and
-- src:3292 | (c) all appointments at the meeting are deemed valid.
