§ `General (ss 258 and 259)`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 258 Power to increase financial limits
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- (1) and (2) are the Secretary of State's order-making power and its parliamentary procedure (machinery). The sums in this Part (ss 207, 211(7), 221) are encoded
-- as the Act states them; a larger sum substituted by an order would change those answers (NOTES.md). (3) says what an order does not reach: encoded.
-- src:3373 | (3) An order does not have effect in relation to anything done or not done before it comes into force.
-- src:3374 | Accordingly, proceedings in respect of any liability incurred before that time may be continued or instituted as if the order had not been made.
@ref s 258(3) an order does not reach what was done before it (src:3373-3374)
GIVEN `the date the thing was done or not done` IS A DATE
      `the date the order comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 258(3) an order under this section has effect in relation to the thing done or not done` MEANS
    IF `the date the thing was done or not done` LESS THAN `the date the order comes into force`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order does not have effect in relation to anything done or not done before it comes into force. Accordingly, proceedings in respect of any liability incurred before that time may be continued or instituted as if the order had not been made"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what a later order provides is not in the sources

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 259 Transactions under foreign law
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:3376 | For the purposes of this Part it is immaterial whether the law that (apart from this Act) governs an arrangement or transaction is the law of the United Kingdom, or a part of it, or not.
@ref s 259 the governing law is immaterial (src:3376-3376)
`s 259 it matters whether the law that governs the arrangement or transaction is the law of the United Kingdom, or a part of it, or not` MEANS
    JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of this Part it is immaterial whether the law that (apart from this Act) governs an arrangement or transaction is the law of the United Kingdom, or a part of it, or not"
